    "media:imagetext": "LIFE PRESERVER\nLife preservers, if needed, are located under each\nseat.\nTO PREPARE FOR A LANDING ON WATER\n1. Follow instructions of crew.\n2. Pull on Life Preserver (see instructions with Life\nPreserver).\n3. Assume bracing position (see diagram).\n4. After plane stops completely, unfasten seat belt.\nFollow instructions of crew.\n5. After leaving plane, inflate Life Preserver.\nEMERGENCY EXIT OPERATION\nFIRE EXTINGUISHER\nAND CRASH AX\nNORMAL EXIT\n• UNLOCKED\nLOCKED\nCLOSE DOOR\nTURN TO LOCK\nPASSENGER DOOR OPERATION\n1. Rotate handle in direction of arrow.\n2. Push door OUT.\nCLUSEU\nWINDOW EMERGENCY EXIT\n1. Grab HATCH HANDLE. Pull handle and entire\nhatch INWARD AND UP clear of opening.\nEMERGENCY EXIT\nEMERGENCY EXIT\n2. Rotate hatch 90 degrees and extend bottom\nthrough opening. Throw outside, aircraft.\nCAUTION\nDO NOT HANDLE OR ATTEMPT TO OPEN THE PASSENGER\nDOOR OR WINDOW EMERGENCY EXITS UNLESS THEY ARE\nTO BE USED IN AN EMERGENCY.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT - SEE OTHER SIDE\nFIRE EXTINGUISHER\nUNDER SEAT",
